Minato's patch to frameworks/base's media/java/android/media/SoundPool.java at android-15.0.0_r1 (Apache-2.0), the
compatibility plan's gap 13 (SoundPool): the static initializer loads no libsoundpool.

Why: Android's SoundPool natives live in libmedia_jni's neighbour libsoundpool, which the static initializer loads.
Minato builds no libsoundpool; its SoundPool natives are libandroid_runtime's (framework/native/android_runtime/
android_media_SoundPool.cpp), registered with the framework's others when the process starts, so the load would throw
UnsatisfiedLinkError out of <clinit> and every use of the class would fail.

--- a/media/java/android/media/SoundPool.java
+++ b/media/java/android/media/SoundPool.java
@@ -115,5 +115,5 @@
  */
 public class SoundPool extends PlayerBase {
-    static { System.loadLibrary("soundpool"); }
+    // Minato: the natives are libandroid_runtime's (android_media_SoundPool.cpp), registered at the start.
 
     // SoundPool messages
